WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.432
The cost of a join depends partly on the size and distribution of the two inputs.

00:00:05.432 --> 00:00:12.462
If both inputs are large, Spark may need to shuffle substantial amounts of data by the join key.

00:00:12.462 --> 00:00:20.012
If one input is genuinely small, Spark may be able to broadcast that smaller table to the workers.

00:00:20.012 --> 00:00:27.137
Think of a small lookup table, such as a short list of department codes, being copied to the workers instead of moving

00:00:27.137 --> 00:00:30.364
the much larger fact table around.

00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:34.945
Do not assume a particular strategy will always be used.

00:00:34.945 --> 00:00:43.155
Filter unnecessary rows, choose only needed columns when it is safe, and inspect the execution plan to see what Spark

00:00:43.155 --> 00:00:44.992
actually intends to do.
